  "description": "The Moon makes no light of its own: the Sun always lights the half facing it, and depending on where it is in its orbit we see more or less of that half. The cycle lasts about 29.5 days, and we always see the same face because the Moon spins once per orbit. Original 3D animation; not to scale.",
